					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calamityheart" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1973848); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1973848&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605883890" alt="CalamityHeart" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1973848)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calamityheart" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1973848); return false;" >CalamityHeart</a></span> <span class="odate time_1525093497 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Apr 2018 13:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3785194">
									

<p>I think your image might be broken; I'm not able to see it.</p>
<p>I won't worry about that, though. This is a curious little thing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3693 can only be seen by observers when their eyes are closed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is the line that hooked me. It's such a simple effect, but it's unique. I haven't seen anything in recent memory that had the same kind of effect. And the image it presents, of a floating statue staring you in the face amidst almost <em>total</em> darkness, is cool and slightly unsettling.</p>
<p>I'm unsure why this is Euclid, though. It only reacts when people observe it with their eyes closed, and is otherwise inert. At least, that's what I assumed to be the case. I'm confused why this thing requires constant supervision, and why it isn't Safe. I've read over it a few times, but I can't really begin to come up with an answer.</p>
<p>The discovery log, while mostly benign, did give this thing a little bit more mystery.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After securing SCP-3693 and moving it off-site, Foundation agents returned to the warehouse to continue their examination of the site. The basement could no longer be located.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Curious. I'm not sure what the implications are here, but it does seem like there's a little more to this simple statue than what's in the document.</p>
<p>Gonna novote this one. A little brief and bare for my liking, but I did enjoy the concept and what substance was there. Not enough to upvote, though.</p>

